  "question": {
    "text": "A magnetic needle is placed in a uniform magnetic field and is aligned with the field. The needle is now rotated by an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ and the work done is $W$. The torque on the magnetic needle at this position is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "je67h",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{3} w$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KI1MN",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3} w$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YiTBN",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} w$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Xvtbl",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\mathrm{W}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, work done $=W$ and $\\theta=60^{\\circ}$ We know that\r\nHence,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nW=M B(1-\\cos \\theta) \\\\\r\nW=M B\\left(1-\\cos 60^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\\r\nW=\\frac{M B}{2} \\\\\r\n|\\tau|=M B \\sin 60^{\\circ}=\\sqrt{3} W\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
